<title>AUSTRALIA: Most CBA branches open despite stop-work.</title>
<headline>Most CBA branches open despite stop-work.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commonwealth Bank of Australia expects around two thirds of branches across Australia to remain open on Monday despite nation-wide stop work meetings by members of the Finance Sector Union (FSU).</p>
<p>&quot;Whilst customers will notice some disruption, due the industrial action by the Fiannce Sector Union, we are pleased at the concern shown by our staff to minimising disruptions to customers,&quot; Lyndell Fraser, head of the bank's Group Corporate Relations, said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The FSU has said more than 25,000 members would participate in the stop work meetings between 9 a.m. and 10.30 a.m. (2300-0030 GMT) to discuss a proposed contract which the union says pares back the rights of bank employees.</p>
<p>Electronic banking is unaffected.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
